From 3fbfd31ab2885bd5054acfeb4ccbb7a680815202 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:47:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] qcom_spmi: Qualcomm SPMI PMIC arbiter v5, PON keys, RTC

The arbiter (qcom,spmi-pmic-arb, version 5) as a bus of PMICs, each a
bus of its peripherals, with register access for peripheral drivers
(qcom_spmi.h) and the interrupt controller for <sid pid irq type>.
After Linux's spmi-pmic-arb: the APID map and owners from the
arbiter's tables, reads through the observer channels, writes through
the read/write channels.

qcom_pon: power key and RESIN through evdev, the power key also
through devctl. qcom_rtc: the PMIC's seconds counter plus an offset
handed over as hint.qcom_rtc.0.offset, since phones such as the Pro1X
cannot set the counter.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sys/conf/files.arm64          |   3 +
 sys/dev/qcom_spmi/qcom_pon.c  | 219 +++++++++
 sys/dev/qcom_spmi/qcom_rtc.c  | 143 ++++++
 sys/dev/qcom_spmi/qcom_spmi.c | 880 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 sys/dev/qcom_spmi/qcom_spmi.h |  30 ++
 5 files changed, 1275 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 sys/dev/qcom_spmi/qcom_pon.c
 create mode 100644 sys/dev/qcom_spmi/qcom_rtc.c
 create mode 100644 sys/dev/qcom_spmi/qcom_spmi.c
 create mode 100644 sys/dev/qcom_spmi/qcom_spmi.h

